(6755181, 1011370, 86447, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Judi:</b></div><hr/><i> $1500-00 a set????  Whoa....you are the rip-off queen, when you can purchase a custom set for less than $5-00 a set....lmao!!!  Although as I said before the challenge started....it would be a great idea to the set available to DPCérs!  Congrats on ribboning. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m positive that that was a joke... sarcasm... just for fun... a lark.   :D<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Judi: $1500-00 a set????  Whoa....you are the rip-off queen, when you can purchase a custom set for less than $5-00 a set....lmao!!!  Although as I said before the challenge started....it would be a great idea to the set available to DPCérs!  Congrats on ribboning.   I''m positive that that was a joke... sarcasm... just for fun... a lark.   :D', '2012-04-30 04:15:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6755187, 1011370, 72318, '<td valign="top">Picture yourself as a non-DPCer looking at this photo purely from a photographical perspective.  What score then would you honestly give this photo?   - who are those people and why are they relevant to the photo?<br/> <br/>Yes it is technically a good (not great) photo but this isnt an arts and crafts / make-a-nod-to-other-DPC-members challenge... that is a dig at the voters btw not the photographer - even she recognises that there was nothing creative in the set-up: "then couldn''t figure out anything creative to do with them. So it''s a straight forward solitaire shot."<br/> <br/>Food for thought.  But congrats on the Blue :)</td>', 'Picture yourself as a non-DPCer looking at this photo purely from a photographical perspective.  What score then would you honestly give this photo?   - who are those people and why are they relevant to the photo? Yes it is technically a good (not great) photo but this isnt an arts and crafts / make-a-nod-to-other-DPC-members challenge... that is a dig at the voters btw not the photographer - even she recognises that there was nothing creative in the set-up: "then couldn''t figure out anything creative to do with them. So it''s a straight forward solitaire shot." Food for thought.  But congrats on the Blue :)', '2012-04-30 04:34:37.000000', NULL, 0),
